  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Kingdom&#x2019;s Resettlement Scheme (UKRS) and Mandate Scheme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to resettle around 3,000 refugees who are categorised as meeting one of UNHCR&#x2019;s seven resettlement submission categories. The caseload is determined in discussion with UNHCR and in line with their projected global resettlement needs. For this project, IOM is facilitating video/telephone interviewing, provision of pre-migration health activities (i.e. migration health activities, and pre-embarkation checks to establish fitness to travel), three-day pre-departure cultural orientation (UKCO) sessions, facilitation of the visa/travel document processing, and providing movement management and operational support to the final destination including operational and/or medical escorts and the delivery of information sessions to local authorities, community sponsors, and other relevant resettlement stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
